{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792943492,"nonce":"Jg4/5TuC0uJl/s51puSvHExqgyc=","title":"A frame in a nested loop never leaves Cranelift for LLVM, so mandelbrot gets no LLVM benefit","message":"Reported on the CI table: mandelbrot hybrid-auto shows tiers 5/0 (five Cranelift installs, no LLVM) and 665 ms; Ash AOT runs the same program in ~330 ms.\n\nCause: the re-tier exit is only placed at an un-nested leaf loop (retier_worth_polling). Mandelbrot's work is one constructor with nested loops (rows, columns, up to 1000 escape iterations). The interpreter hands the frame to the Cranelift OSR entry rooted at the inner loop, which proposes LLVM; LLVM builds an exit for the only eligible loop, the palette loop at the top, and the frame, now inside the nest, has no exit to take. The function-level LLVM install is deferred as 'handed-off' (nothing calls the function again), so tiers read 5/0 and the frame stays in Cranelift. Long-standing: older binaries behave the same.\n\nAn OSR entry rooted at header H contains the outer loops only as non-natural cycles (the entry bypasses their headers), so an exit at an outer header never exists in the body the frame runs. Exits on every leaf loop of a body (tried, ASH_RETIER_NESTED=leaf) worked but cost fannkuchredux +15% on the NUC: each extra site keeps 13-17 values live in a hot inner loop.\n\nFix: an OSR entry also carries the exit for its own header when that header is a leaf loop, nested or not; bodies keep the old rule. At most one extra site per entry, in the loop the frame is actually in.\n\nNUC, quiet, 15 interleaved runs, medians vs default (all-leaf / entry-rooted): spectralnorm -9.6% / -20.1%; mandelbrot -22.7% / -9.4% (best run -21%); fasta -4.3% / -3.1%; fannkuchredux +15.0% / +5.0%; pidigits, nbody, deltablue, knucleotide within 2%. Runs are bimodal: in the fast mode the exit is taken while the ~200 ms LLVM entry build is still in time. Mac gave mandelbrot -37%, spectralnorm -11%. Output identical on all 16 kernels.\n\nTest: osr_retier::a_frame_in_a_nested_loop_leaves_through_its_own_loops_exit forces the hand-off with ASH_TEST_RETIER_AFTER on the TestOsrNested fixture.\n\nOpen: the fannkuchredux +5% (extra sites in hot Cranelift loops), and the LLVM entry build time that decides how early the exit is taken.","files":null}]}